92186045443 true] [17592186671790 1077 "selection" 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671790 1078 #edb/ref 17592186671797 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671790 1079 #uuid "95db082d-c26f-5c7b-b38f-fad722cb20af" 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671791 1080 "No solution" 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671791 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671791 1083 #uuid "b7848208-b871-5a17-84b1-3b9c6807c229" 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671792 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3y+4 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671792 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671792 1083 #uuid "bf4109ee-8abb-55ff-a747-7f28815c182e" 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671793 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-y-12 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671793 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671793 1083 #uuid "cd5338fa-f2d5-5f21-9ced-a4cbb650a386" 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671794 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4y-4 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671794 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671794 1083 #uuid "d54b6829-c036-5c86-b2c1-d6fd61c6ff36" 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671795 1068 #edb/ref 17592186671790 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671795 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671795 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=6 \\\\ -4x+8y &=-24.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671795 1072 #uuid "d57ed010-daa6-567c-bb10-67266ffc6276" 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671795 1074 "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -24\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -24\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & \\sim\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=6 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-2y=6.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=2y+6,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2y+6 \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2y+6 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671796 1068 #edb/ref 17592186671788 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671796 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671796 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y &=-6 \\\\ 2x+6y &=-7.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671796 1072 #uuid "f3181108-6901-544f-bc34-d0fa3617da7b" 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671796 1074 "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -7\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \\sim\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y &=-6 \\\\ 0x+0y &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=5$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=5,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution." 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671797 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2y+6 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671797 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671797 1083 #uuid "f3c673c5-f4c0-5d0d-bb51-b280f48a19e2" 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671798 1080 "No solution" 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671798 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671798 1083 #uuid "f704f18e-d06d-5324-965f-8b94ff5810d2" 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671799 1068 #edb/ref 17592186671783 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671799 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139538677 17592186045443 true] [17592186671799 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=-8 \\\\ -3x+6y &=30.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of th